<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n520" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁγίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅγιος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hallow, make sacred,</i>
			esp. by burning a sacrifice, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῷ βούθυτον ἑστίαν ἁγίζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1495
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόπανα ἥγιζεν ἐς
			σάκταν</span> (for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς βωμόν</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				681
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμοὶ πατρὶ ἁγισθέντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					3.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύματα ἐπὶ καθαρῷ πυρὶ-όμενα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.38
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅζομαι.</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				123
			</span></i>.</div>
